NAME
    sysgen - install a kernel in the boot sectors

SYNOPSIS
    sysgen file

DESCRIPTION
    Writes a kernel to the reserved sectors LBA 1.. of this disk, reads
    each one back, then sets OSCNT in the boot block: on the machine
    what `p8xfs.py boot` does on the Mac. The running OS stays in
    memory; the new kernel starts at the next O. sysgen is /bin/sysgen.

    The file is a program file with load and exec $1000, as

        asm y1os.asm y1os

    writes it. /lib/y1os is the kernel the disk was built with. In
    /src/os, make boot builds y1os and runs sysgen on it.

LIMITS
    32 sectors (16K) at most. There is one copy of the kernel: a
    failure half way leaves a card that does not boot, until the kernel
    is written again from the Mac (docs/procedures/CF-CARD.md).
    Messages: "sysgen: not found", "sysgen: not a kernel: load and exec
    must be $1000", "sysgen: an empty file", "sysgen: over 32 sectors",
    "sysgen: no P8XFS boot block", and the CF errors. Each ends with
    status 1, so a running script stops.

EXAMPLES
    sysgen /lib/y1os       the installed kernel again
    cd /src/os
    make boot              a kernel built here

NOTES
    Added 2026-11-05 (os/commands/sysgen.c).

